-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct pre- and post-restart behavioral evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart boot ID corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and recovered services, listeners, firewall state, and responses. The only notable hygiene defect is the retained, unrequested nginx listener on TCP 80.","limitations":["The TCP 8090 request originated on node1 using its network address rather than from an independent external client; the all-interface listener and runtime/permanent firewalld rule strongly support publication.","The evidence does not query whether firewalld exposes the unintended TCP 80 listener, so its actual off-node reachability is indeterminate.","The standalone task has no durable application data or multi-node cluster state to validate during the restart protocol; all applicable service and network state was verified."]}
